  "term": "orthotics",
  "definition": "Orthotics are custom-made medical devices used to protect, correct, and support the body in people with conditions that affect movement or physical development. They are typically adjusted over time as a person’s body or recovery changes, because poor fit can cause pain, skin problems, or reduced mobility.",
